  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 148 AM CDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\nAn elongated east/west oriented ridge stretching from the southern\nplains to the eastern seaboard remains in place through the middle\nof the week preventing any significant change in temperatures.\nModels are indicating a trough moving across the upper Midwest\nerodes the eastern portion of the ridge, reorienting it back to\nthe western United States. The current NBM does not show this\nchange affecting the sensible weather in our CWA for next weekend\nthough it is hard to see how lower heights and reduced subsidence\nwould not be favorable for at least slightly cooler temperatures. \n\nHennig",
